description:
It's linked to "How to make sure that my code works with the real API?" but is something linked to the package code outside of tests. I'd find something like the tip below very helpful.

````markdown
With presser you will spin up fake services and you will want your package to connect to that rather than the real web API.
How to make it as smooth as possible?

Instead of simply hard-coding the URL of web services your code is interacting with, use a function returning it, and make sure you can change the output of that function with an environment variable or option.

E.g.

```r
service_url <- function() {
	if(nzchar(Sys.getenv("SERVICE_URL")) {
		return(Sys.getenv("SERVICE_URL"))
	}
	return("https://service.url")
}

# rest of the package code

foobar <- function() {
	httr::GET(service_url())
}

```

And then in tests you'd set the environment variable `SERVICE_URL` to be the url of the app you are running.

````
